[1m[38;5;231mWhat should actually generate a notification?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mTime events via event bus (Rec.)[39m
     [38;5;246mDue/overdue/reminder events are what surface; edit events exist as a second producer on a shared bus so a future [39m
     [38;5;246mbackend plugs in as a third.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Time-crossing events only
     [38;5;246mDue dates, overdue, reminders. No event bus abstraction — simplest thing that carries real information.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m User's own edits only
     [38;5;246mCompleted/moved/deleted show as toasts or a feed. No clock, no permissions. I'd call this an activity log, not [39m
     [38;5;246mnotifications.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m Both, no shared abstraction
     [38;5;246mTime events and edit events, each wired directly to the UI. Fastest to write, hardest to extend.[39m
